-hidden="true"><path d="M13.9,10.5L21.1,2h-1.7l-6.3,7.4L8,2H2.2l7.6,11.1L2.2,22h1.7l6.7-7.8L16,22h5.8L13.9,10.5L13.9,10.5z M11.5,13.2l-0.8-1.1 L4.6,3.3h2.7l5,7.1l0.8,1.1l6.5,9.2h-2.7L11.5,13.2L11.5,13.2z"></path></svg></a></li><li class="hpHPGf"><a class="nRhiJb-ARYxNe" href="https://www.linkedin.com/shareArticle?mini=true&amp;url=https://cloud.google.com/blog/products/data-analytics/using-bigquerys-generative-ai-cost-management-features&amp;title=Predictable%20AI%20spend%20in%20BigQuery:%20Introducing%20cost%20management%20for%20generative%20AI%20functions" track-name="linkedin"track-type="social share"track-metadata-eventdetail="www.linkedin.com/shareArticle?mini=true&amp;url=cloud.google.com/blog/products/data-analytics/using-bigquerys-generative-ai-cost-management-features&amp;title=Predictable AI spend in BigQuery: Introducing cost management for generative AI functions"track-metadata-module="social icons" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="nRhiJb-Bz112c nRhiJb-Bz112c-OWXEXe-DX2B6 nRhiJb-Bz112c-OWXEXe-nSuQf" viewBox="0 0 24 24" role="presentation" aria-hidden="true" role="presentation" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 2H4c-1.1 0-1.99.9-1.99 2L2 20c0 1.1.9 2 2 2h16c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2V4c0-1.1-.9-2-2-2zM8 19H5v-9h3v9zM6.5 8.31c-1 0-1.81-.81-1.81-1.81S5.5 4.69 6.5 4.69s1.81.81 1.81 1.81S7.5 8.31 6.5 8.31zM19 19h-3v-5.3c0-.83-.67-1.5-1.5-1.5s-1.5.67-1.5 1.5V19h-3v-9h3v1.2c.52-.84 1.59-1.4 2.5-1.4 1.93 0 3.5 1.57 3.5 3.5V19z"></path></svg></a></li><li class="hpHPGf"><a class="nRhiJb-ARYxNe" href="https://www.facebook.com/sharer/sharer.php?caption=Predictable%20AI%20spend%20in%20BigQuery:%20Introducing%20cost%20management%20for%20generative%20AI%20functions&amp;u=https://cloud.google.com/blog/products/data-analytics/using-bigquerys-generative-ai-cost-management-features" track-name="facebook"track-type="social share"track-metadata-eventdetail="www.facebook.com/sharer/sharer.php?caption=Predictable AI spend in BigQuery: Introducing cost management for generative AI functions&amp;u=cloud.google.com/blog/products/data-analytics/using-bigquerys-generative-ai-cost-management-features"track-metadata-module="social icons" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="nRhiJb-Bz112c nRhiJb-Bz112c-OWXEXe-DX2B6 nRhiJb-Bz112c-OWXEXe-nSuQf" viewBox="0 0 24 24" role="presentation" aria-hidden="true" role="presentation" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 2H4c-1.1 0-1.99.9-1.99 2L2 20c0 1.1.9 2 2 2h16c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2V4c0-1.1-.9-2-2-2zm-1 2v3h-2c-.55 0-1 .45-1 1v2h3v3h-3v7h-3v-7h-2v-3h2V7.5C13 5.57 14.57 4 16.5 4H19z"></path></svg></a></li><li class="hpHPGf"><a class="nRhiJb-ARYxNe" href="mailto:?subject=Predictable%20AI%20spend%20in%20BigQuery:%20Introducing%20cost%20management%20for%20generative%20AI%20functions&amp;body=Check%20out%20this%20article%20on%20the%20Cloud%20Blog:%0A%0APredictable%20AI%20spend%20in%20BigQuery:%20Introducing%20cost%20management%20for%20generative%20AI%20functions%0A%0AToken-based%20cost%20management%20for%20BigQuery%20generative%20AI%20functions%20lets%20you%20set%20daily%20quotas%20on%20AI%20token%20consumption%20so%20you%20can%20keep%20within%20your%20budget.%0A%0Ahttps://cloud.google.com/blog/products/data-analytics/using-bigquerys-generative-ai-cost-management-features" track-name="email"track-type="social share"track-metadata-eventdetail="mailto:?subject=Predictable AI spend in BigQuery: Introducing cost management for generative AI functions&amp;body=Check%20out%20this%20article%20on%20the%20Cloud%20Blog:%0A%0APredictable AI spend in BigQuery: Introducing cost management for generative AI functions%0A%0AToken-based cost management for BigQuery generative AI functions lets you set daily quotas on AI token consumption so you can keep within your budget.%0A%0Acloud.google.com/blog/products/data-analytics/using-bigquerys-generative-ai-cost-management-features"track-metadata-module="social icons" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="nRhiJb-Bz112c nRhiJb-Bz112c-OWXEXe-DX2B6 nRhiJb-Bz112c-OWXEXe-nSuQf" viewBox="0 0 24 24" role="presentation" aria-hidden="true" role="presentation" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 4H4c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v12c0 1.1.9 2 2 2h16c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2V6c0-1.1-.9-2-2-2zm-.8 2L12 10.8 4.8 6h14.4zM4 18V7.87l8 5.33 8-5.33V18H4z"></path></svg></a></li></ul></div></div></div></div></div><div><section class="nRhiJb-DARUcf"><div class="nRhiJb-DbgRPb-wNfPc-ma6Yeb nRhiJb-DbgRPb-wNfPc-cGMI2b"><section class="DA9Qj nRhiJb-ObfsIf nRhiJb-fmcmS-oXtfBe"><div class="nRhiJb-kR0ZEf-OWXEXe-GV1x9e-ibL1re"></div><div class="nRhiJb-kR0ZEf-OWXEXe-GV1x9e-II5mzb kWSSdd"><h5 class="cHE8Ub Qwf2Db-MnozTc Qwf2Db-MnozTc-OWXEXe-MnozTc-qWD73c">Tushar Jaiswal</h5><p class="nRhiJb-qJTHM khCp7b">Software Engineer</p></div><div class="nRhiJb-kR0ZEf-OWXEXe-GV1x9e-II5mzb kWSSdd"><h5 class="cHE8Ub Qwf2Db-MnozTc Qwf2Db-MnozTc-OWXEXe-MnozTc-qWD73c">Alicia Williams</h5><p class="nRhiJb-qJTHM khCp7b">Developer Advocate</p></div></section></div></section><div class="nRhiJb-DARUcf"><div class="nRhiJb-ObfsIf nRhiJb-DbgRPb-wNfPc-ma6Yeb nRhiJb-DbgRPb-qWD73c-cGMI2b"><div class="nRhiJb-kR0ZEf-OWXEXe-GV1x9e-ibL1re dzoHJ"><div class="aLW4J" track-metadata-module="left rail"><h5 class="qZDXV Qwf2Db-MnozTc Qwf2Db-MnozTc-OWXEXe-MnozTc-wNfPc">Nov 4: Agentic Data Cloud Event</h5><p class="nRhiJb-cHYyed Mrfygc nRhiJb-BP2Omd-ma6Yeb-KE6vqe nRhiJb-DbgRPb-R6PoUb-cGMI2b">Join our product leaders to architect your agentic future</p><a class="nRhiJb-LgbsSe  nRhiJb-LgbsSe-OWXEXe-CNusmb-o6Shpd " href="https://cloudonair.withgoogle.com/events/trusted-agents-real-outcomes-agentic-data-cloud?utm_source=blog&amp;utm_campaign=FY26-Q4-GLOBAL-STO891-onlineevent-er-agntc-dc-lv-251895&amp;utm_content=blog&amp;" track-metadata-module="left rail"track-metadata-module_headline="nov 4: agentic data cloud event" track-name="register"track-type="button"track-metadata-position="cta"track-metadata-eventdetail="cloudonair.withgoogle.com/events/trusted-agents-real-outcomes-agentic-data-cloud?utm_source=blog&amp;utm_campaign=FY26-Q4-GLOBAL-STO891-onlineevent-er-agntc-dc-lv-251895&amp;utm_content=blog&amp;">Register </a></div></div><div class="OYL9D nRhiJb-kR0ZEf-OWXEXe-GV1x9e-OiUrBf" jsname="tx2NYc"><section class="Wy08Ac nRhiJb-qJTHM-OWXEXe-hJDwNd nRhiJb-DbgRPb-II5mzb-cGMI2b"><div jsaction="rcuQ6b:npT2md" jscontroller="M0Q3Qb" data-is-cws-richtext="true" class=" "><p><span style="vertical-align:baseline">The </span><a href="https://docs.cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/generative-ai-overview"><span style="text-decoration:underline;vertical-align:baseline">generative AI functions in BigQuery</span></a><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> (</span><code style="vertical-align:baseline">AI.GENERATE</code><span style="vertical-align:baseline">, </span><code style="vertical-align:baseline">AI.IF</code><span style="vertical-align:baseline">, </span><code style="vertical-align:baseline">AI.CLASSIFY</code><span style="vertical-align:baseline">, </span><code style="vertical-align:baseline">AI.SCORE</code><span style="vertical-align:baseline">, and more) bring large language models (LLMs) directly into your SQL, so a single query can classify millions of support tickets or score each product review for sentiment. However, because these functions are billed by the token, scaling them across massive datasets highlights the importance of managing your budget proactively. </span></p>
<p><span style="vertical-align:baseline">We recently announced the general availability (GA) of </span><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">token-based </strong><a href="https://docs.cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/control-genai-costs"><strong style="text-decoration:underline;vertical-align:baseline">cost management</strong></a><strong style="vertical-align:baseline"> for BigQuery generative AI functions</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline">: daily quotas that let administrators set self-serve guardrails on AI token consumption, so teams can innovate while staying within your budget. In this blog, we provide an overview of cost management for BigQuery generative AI functions, walk through a few practical examples, and share resources to help you get started. Let’s jump in.  </span></p>
<h3><span style="vertical-align:baseline">Quotas for managing costs</span></h3>
<p><span style="vertical-align:baseline">Four daily quotas, managed through the Google Cloud Identity and Access Management (IAM) quota system, provide controls at the </span><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">project</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> level and the </span><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">per-user</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> level. Per-user limits apply to each user within a project, not across your organization.<br><br></span></p>
<div align="left">
<div style="color:#5f6368;overflow-x:auto;overflow-y:hidden;width:100%">
<div style="color:#5f6368;overflow-x:auto;overflow-y:hidden;width:100%">
<div style="color:#5f6368;overflow-x:auto;overflow-y:hidden;width:100%">
<div style="color:#5f6368;overflow-x:auto;overflow-y:hidden;width:100%">
<div style="color:#5f6368;overflow-x:auto;overflow-y:hidden;width:100%">
<div style="color:#5f6368;overflow-x:auto;overflow-y:hidden;width:100%"><table><colgroup><col><col><col><col></colgroup>
<thead>
<tr>
<th style="vertical-align:top;border:1px solid #000000;padding:16px">
