</tbody>
</table></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><span style="vertical-align:baseline">Key details:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="list-style-type:disc;vertical-align:baseline">
<p><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">The quotas are global.</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> Usage is summed across all regions, so costs can't pile up unnoticed in a region you weren't watching.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="list-style-type:disc;vertical-align:baseline">
<p><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">Output quotas include "thinking" tokens.</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> Reasoning tokens count toward your output quota, just as they count toward your Gemini platform bill.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3><span style="vertical-align:baseline">Which functions are covered?</span></h3>
<p><span style="vertical-align:baseline">The quotas apply to these BigQuery functions that perform LLM-backed generation:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="list-style-type:disc;vertical-align:baseline">
<p><a href="https://docs.cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/standard-sql/bigqueryml-syntax-ai-generate"><code style="text-decoration:underline;vertical-align:baseline">AI.GENERATE</code></a></p>
</li>
<li style="list-style-type:disc;vertical-align:baseline">
<p><a href="https://docs.cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/standard-sql/bigqueryml-syntax-generate-table"><code style="text-decoration:underline;vertical-align:baseline">AI.GENERATE_TABLE</code></a></p>
</li>
<li style="list-style-type:disc;vertical-align:baseline">
<p><a href="https://docs.cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/standard-sql/bigqueryml-syntax-ai-generate-text"><code style="text-decoration:underline;vertical-align:baseline">AI.GENERATE_TEXT</code></a><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> (and its alias </span><a href="https://docs.cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/standard-sql/bigqueryml-syntax-generate-text"><code style="text-decoration:underline;vertical-align:baseline">ML.GENERATE_TEXT</code></a><span style="vertical-align:baseline">)</span></p>
</li>
<li style="list-style-type:disc;vertical-align:baseline">
<p><a href="https://docs.cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/standard-sql/bigqueryml-syntax-ai-classify"><code style="text-decoration:underline;vertical-align:baseline">AI.CLASSIFY</code></a></p>
</li>
<li style="list-style-type:disc;vertical-align:baseline">
<p><a href="https://docs.cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/standard-sql/bigqueryml-syntax-ai-if"><code style="text-decoration:underline;vertical-align:baseline">AI.IF</code></a></p>
</li>
<li style="list-style-type:disc;vertical-align:baseline">
<p><a href="https://docs.cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/standard-sql/bigqueryml-syntax-ai-score"><code style="text-decoration:underline;vertical-align:baseline">AI.SCORE</code></a></p>
</li>
<li style="list-style-type:disc;vertical-align:baseline">
<p><a href="https://docs.cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/standard-sql/bigqueryml-syntax-ai-agg"><code style="text-decoration:underline;vertical-align:baseline">AI.AGG</code></a></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">What's not covered:</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> Embedding functions such as </span><a href="https://docs.cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/standard-sql/bigqueryml-syntax-generate-text"><code style="text-decoration:underline;vertical-align:baseline">AI.GENERATE_EMBEDDING</code></a><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> (also available as </span><a href="https://docs.cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/standard-sql/bigqueryml-syntax-generate-embedding"><code style="text-decoration:underline;vertical-align:baseline">ML.GENERATE_EMBEDDING</code></a><span style="vertical-align:baseline">) and </span><a href="https://docs.cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/standard-sql/bigqueryml-syntax-ai-embed"><code style="text-decoration:underline;vertical-align:baseline">AI.EMBED</code></a><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> are </span><span style="font-style:italic;vertical-align:baseline">not</span><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> subject to these quotas, because they run on different, substantially cheaper models.</span></p>
<h3><span style="vertical-align:baseline">Managing your quotas</span></h3>
<p><span style="vertical-align:baseline">Administrators can view and adjust the quotas directly in the </span><a href="https://docs.cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/control-genai-costs"><span style="text-decoration:underline;vertical-align:baseline">Google Cloud console</span></a><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> as workloads change, with no support case required.</span></p>
<ol>
<li style="list-style-type:decimal;vertical-align:baseline">
<p><span style="vertical-align:baseline">Navigate to </span><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">IAM &amp; Admin → </strong><a href="https://console.cloud.google.com/iam-admin/quotas/list"><strong style="text-decoration:underline;vertical-align:baseline">Quotas &amp; System Limits</strong></a><span style="vertical-align:baseline">.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="list-style-type:decimal;vertical-align:baseline">
<p><span style="vertical-align:baseline">Filter by service and select </span><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">BigQuery API</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline">.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="list-style-type:decimal;vertical-align:baseline">
<p><span style="vertical-align:baseline">Sort by the </span><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">Name</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> column to bring the four AI quotas to the top.</span></p>
</li>
</ol></div></section><section class="QzPuud"><div><section><figure class="NEBdNd"><section class="PBkdHd DhGbH" jscontroller="SCGBie" jsaction="rcuQ6b:npT2md"><img class="JcsBte mZzdH ZOnyjc" src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-cloudblog-publish/images/1_dxxy8WS.max-2000x2000.png" alt="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-cloudblog-publish/images/1_dxxy8WS.max-2000x2000.png" jsname='P3Vluc' jsaction="click:HTIlC" loading="lazy"/><section class="glue-modal glue-modal--dark QHdDac" role="dialog" aria-modal="true"><img class="JcsBte mZzdH ZOnyjc" src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-cloudblog-publish/images/1_dxxy8WS.max-2000x2000.png" alt="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-cloudblog-publish/images/1_dxxy8WS.max-2000x2000.png" jsname='P3Vluc' jsaction="click:HTIlC" loading="lazy"/><button class="glue-modal__close-btn" tabindex="0" aria-label="Close this modal"></button></section></section></figure><div class="nRhiJb-cHYyed nRhiJb-DbgRPb-R6PoUb-ma6Yeb ZpqjUe"><div jsaction="rcuQ6b:npT2md" jscontroller="M0Q3Qb" data-is-cws-richtext="true" class=" "><p>Locating the gen AI token quotas in IAM &amp; Admin → Quotas &amp; System Limits.</p></div></div></section></div></section><section class="Wy08Ac nRhiJb-qJTHM-OWXEXe-hJDwNd nRhiJb-DbgRPb-II5mzb-cGMI2b"><div jsaction="rcuQ6b:npT2md" jscontroller="M0Q3Qb" data-is-cws-richtext="true" class=" "><p><span style="vertical-align:baseline">4. Find the quota, for example </span><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">AI input tokens per day</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline">.</span></p>
<p><span style="vertical-align:baseline">5. Open the three-dot menu and choose </span><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">Edit quota</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline">.</span></p>
<p><span style="vertical-align:baseline">From there:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="list-style-type:disc;vertical-align:baseline">
<p><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">To tighten cost control,</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> lower a quota. This takes effect immediately with no approval needed.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="list-style-type:disc;vertical-align:baseline">
<p><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">To support higher usage,</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> request an increase from the same page. Many requests are auto-approved; larger increases may go through a quick review.</span></p>
</li>
</ul></div></section><section class="QzPuud"><div><section><figure class="NEBdNd"><section class="PBkdHd DhGbH" jscontroller="SCGBie" jsaction="rcuQ6b:npT2md"><img class="JcsBte mZzdH ZOnyjc" src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-cloudblog-publish/images/2_7NmvWbT.max-2000x2000.png" alt="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-cloudblog-publish/images/2_7NmvWbT.max-2000x2000.png" jsname='P3Vluc' jsaction="click:HTIlC" loading="lazy"/><section class="glue-modal glue-modal--dark QHdDac" role="dialog" aria-modal="true"><img class="JcsBte mZzdH ZOnyjc" src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-cloudblog-publish/images/2_7NmvWbT.max-2000x2000.png" alt="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-cloudblog-publish/images/2_7NmvWbT.max-2000x2000.png" jsname='P3Vluc' jsaction="click:HTIlC" loading="lazy"/><button class="glue-modal__close-btn" tabindex="0" aria-label="Close this modal"></button></section></section></figure><div class="nRhiJb-cHYyed nRhiJb-DbgRPb-R6PoUb-ma6Yeb ZpqjUe"><div jsaction="rcuQ6b:npT2md" jscontroller="M0Q3Qb" data-is-cws-richtext="true" class=" "><p>Editing a gen AI token quota in IAM &amp; Admin → Quotas &amp; System Limits.</p></div></div></section></div></section><section class="Wy08Ac nRhiJb-qJTHM-OWXEXe-hJDwNd nRhiJb-DbgRPb-II5mzb-cGMI2b"><div jsaction="rcuQ6b:npT2md" jscontroller="M0Q3Qb" data-is-cws-richtext="true" class=" "><p><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">You'll need the right permissions.</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> You need one of: </span><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">Owner</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline">, </span><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">Editor, </strong><a href="https://docs.cloud.google.com/iam/docs/roles-permissions/servicemanagement#servicemanagement.quotaAdmin"><strong style="text-decoration:underline;vertical-align:baseline">Quota Administrator</strong><span style="text-decoration:underline;vertical-align:baseline"> </span></a><span style="vertical-align:baseline">(</span><code style="vertical-align:baseline">roles/servicemanagement.quotaAdmin</code><span style="vertical-align:baseline">), or </span><a href="https://docs.cloud.google.com/iam/docs/roles-permissions/serviceusage#serviceusage.serviceUsageAdmin"><strong style="text-decoration:underline;vertical-align:baseline">Service Usage Admin</strong></a><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> (</span><code style="vertical-align:baseline">roles/serviceusage.serviceUsageAdmin</code><span style="vertical-align:baseline">).</span></p>
<p><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">Prefer automation?</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> You can also </span><a href="https://medium.com/google-cloud/bigquery-ai-cost-guardrails-how-to-set-daily-token-limits-programmatically-02d7a35f843a" rel="noopener" target="_blank"><span style="text-decoration:underline;vertical-align:baseline">manage these quotas programmatically</span></a><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> through the </span><a href="https://docs.cloud.google.com/docs/quotas"><span style="text-decoration:underline;vertical-align:baseline">Cloud Quotas API</span></a><span style="vertical-align:baseline">, the </span><code style="vertical-align:baseline">gcloud</code><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> CLI, and Terraform to apply consistent guardrails across projects.</span></p>
<h3><span style="vertical-align:baseline">Monitoring usage</span></h3>
<p><span style="vertical-align:baseline">Beyond setting limits, the </span><a href="https://console.cloud.google.com/iam-admin/quotas/list"><strong style="text-decoration:underline;vertical-align:baseline">Quotas &amp; System Limits</strong></a><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> page displays your historical token consumption so you can quickly detect spikes and right-size your budgets. Use these trends to see how new generative AI workloads and data pipelines affect your overall token usage.</span></p></div></section><section class="QzPuud"><div><section><figure class="NEBdNd"><section class="PBkdHd DhGbH" jscontroller="SCGBie" jsaction="rcuQ6b:npT2md"><img class="JcsBte mZzdH ZOnyjc" src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-cloudblog-publish/images/3_sSNHw57.max-2000x2000.png" alt="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-cloudblog-publish/images/3_sSNHw57.max-2000x2000.png" jsname='P3Vluc' jsaction="click:HTIlC" loading="lazy"/><section class="glue-modal glue-modal--dark QHdDac" role="dialog" aria-modal="true"><img class="JcsBte mZzdH ZOnyjc" src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-cloudblog-publish/images/3_sSNHw57.max-2000x2000.png" alt="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-cloudblog-publish/images/3_sSNHw57.max-2000x2000.png" jsname='P3Vluc' jsaction="click:HTIlC" loading="lazy"/><button class="glue-modal__close-btn" tabindex="0" aria-label="Close this modal"></button></section></section></figure><div class="nRhiJb-cHYyed nRhiJb-DbgRPb-R6PoUb-ma6Yeb ZpqjUe"><div jsaction="rcuQ6b:npT2md" jscontroller="M0Q3Qb" data-is-cws-richtext="true" class=" "><p>Daily project-level token usage for a gen AI token quota in IAM &amp; Admin → Quotas &amp; System Limits.</p></div></div></section></div></section><section class="QzPuud"><div><section><figure class="NEBdNd"><section class="PBkdHd DhGbH" jscontroller="SCGBie" jsaction="rcuQ6b:npT2md"><img class="JcsBte mZzdH ZOnyjc" src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-cloudblog-publish/images/4_iYgfR4l.max-2000x2000.png" alt="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-cloudblog-publish/images/4_iYgfR4l.max-2000x2000.png" jsname='P3Vluc' jsaction="click:HTIlC" loading="lazy"/><section class="glue-modal glue-modal--dark QHdDac" role="dialog" aria-modal="true"><img class="JcsBte mZzdH ZOnyjc" src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-cloudblog-publish/images/4_iYgfR4l.max-2000x2000.png" alt="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-cloudblog-publish/images/4_iYgfR4l.max-2000x2000.png" jsname='P3Vluc' jsaction="click:HTIlC" loading="lazy"/><button class="glue-modal__close-btn" tabindex="0" aria-label="Close this modal"></button></section></section></figure><div class="nRhiJb-cHYyed nRhiJb-DbgRPb-R6PoUb-ma6Yeb ZpqjUe"><div jsaction="rcuQ6b:npT2md" jscontroller="M0Q3Qb" data-is-cws-richtext="true" class=" "><p>Longer-term usage graph with selectable 7-day, 14-day, 30-day, and custom ranges.</p></div></div></section></div></section><section class="Wy08Ac nRhiJb-qJTHM-OWXEXe-hJDwNd nRhiJb-DbgRPb-II5mzb-cGMI2b"><div jsaction="rcuQ6b:npT2md" jscontroller="M0Q3Qb" data-is-cws-richtext="true" class=" "><p><span style="vertical-align:baseline">For a step-by-step walkthrough, see the BigQuery documentation on </span><a href="https://docs.cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/control-genai-costs"><span style="text-decoration:underline;vertical-align:baseline">controlling costs with token quotas</span></a><span style="vertical-align:baseline">.</span></p>
<h3><span style="vertical-align:baseline">Token quotas vs. billing spend caps</span></h3>
<p><span style="vertical-align:baseline">Token quotas aren't the only cost guardrail in Google Cloud.</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="list-style-type:disc;vertical-align:baseline">
<p><a href="https://docs.cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/control-genai-costs"><strong style="text-decoration:underline;vertical-align:baseline">Token quotas (this feature)</strong></a><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> are </span><span style="font-style:italic;vertical-align:baseline">preventive</span><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> and </span><span style="font-style:italic;vertical-align:baseline">AI-specific</span><span style="vertical-align:baseline">. BigQuery tracks token usage during query execution and stops work close to the limit, with separate limits per project and per user.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="list-style-type:disc;vertical-align:baseline">
<p><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">Cloud Billing </strong><a href="https://docs.cloud.google.com/billing/docs/how-to/budgets-spend-caps#eligible-services"><strong style="text-decoration:underline;vertical-align:baseline">spend caps</strong></a><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> operate on </span><span style="font-style:italic;vertical-align:baseline">dollars</span><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> at the project and service level and can automatically block usage when a threshold is reached. They're a broad, financial backstop rather than a precise usage control, and because enforcement is not instant, some overages are incurred.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><span style="vertical-align:baseline">Use token quotas as your first line of defense for AI spend, and a spend cap as a project-wide safety net.</span></p>
<h3><span style="vertical-align:baseline">How enforcement works</span></h3>
<p><span style="vertical-align:baseline">Quotas are enforced by stopping work rather than letting a query run past your limit. A query is rejected up front with a </span><code style="vertical-align:baseline">QuotaExceeded</code><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> error only if a quota it needs is already exhausted. Otherwise, it starts, and if a quota runs out mid-query, BigQuery stops sending new LLM calls:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="list-style-type:disc;vertical-align:baseline">
<p><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">Functions that support </strong><code><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">max_error_ratio</strong></code><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> (such as </span><code style="vertical-align:baseline">AI.IF</code><span style="vertical-align:baseline">) return partial results if unprocessed rows stay within the ratio, and otherwise fail.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="list-style-type:disc;vertical-align:baseline">
<p><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">General-purpose functions</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> (such as </span><code style="vertical-align:baseline">AI.GENERATE</code><span style="vertical-align:baseline">) still succeed. Skipped rows have no generated value, and their </span><code style="vertical-align:baseline">status</code><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> field contains the quota-exceeded error.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><span style="vertical-align:baseline">For details, see </span><a href="https://docs.cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/control-genai-costs#quota_enforcement_behavior"><span style="text-decoration:underline;vertical-align:baseline">quota enforcement behavior</span></a><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> in the documentation.</span></p>
<h3><span style="vertical-align:baseline">Sizing your input data: </span><code style="vertical-align:baseline">AI.COUNT_TOKENS</code></h3>
<p><span style="vertical-align:baseline">To choose quota values, it helps to know how much text your workloads send to a model. The </span><a href="https://docs.cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/standard-sql/bigqueryml-syntax-ai-count-tokens"><code style="text-decoration:underline;vertical-align:baseline">AI.COUNT_TOKENS</code></a><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> function helps with this.</span></p>
<p><code style="vertical-align:baseline">AI.COUNT_TOKENS</code><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> returns the number of tokens a model's tokenizer produces for a text string, without making a billable generation call. Run it over a column to measure your input data:</span></p></div></section><section class="nRhiJb-DbgRPb-II5mzb-cGMI2b"><section><div class="kg99be" jscontroller="vkZm2d" jsaction="rcuQ6b:npT2md" data-text-to-copy="-- Count the input text tokens for each product review
SELECT
  SUM(
    AI.COUNT_TOKENS(
      CONCAT(&#39;Classify the sentiment of this review as positive, negative, or neutral: &#39;, review_text),

      endpoint =&gt; &#39;gemini-3.1-flash-lite&#39;).result) AS total_input_tokens
FROM
  `my_project.my_dataset.product_reviews`;" soy-skip ssk='4:dXrt'><div jsaction="click:VTVhdd" class="GaRnv"><svg class="" viewBox="0 0 20 20" role="presentation" aria-hidden="true" height=20 widdht=20><path d="M7.979 14.667c-.458 0-.84-.153-1.146-.459a1.53 1.53 0 0 1-.458-1.125V3.938c0-.459.153-.84.458-1.146.306-.306.688-.459 1.146-.459h6.625c.445 0 .823.156 1.136.469.312.313.468.691.468 1.136v9.145c0 .445-.156.82-.468 1.125a1.564 1.564 0 0 1-1.136.459H7.979Zm0-1.334h6.625c.083 0 .15-.024.198-.073a.239.239 0 0 0 .073-.177V3.938a.265.265 0 0 0-.073-.198.268.268 0 0 0-.198-.073H7.979a.268.268 0 0 0-.198.073.266.266 0 0 0-.073.198v9.145c0 .07.024.129.073.177a.267.267 0 0 0 .198.073ZM4.875 17.75a1.53 1.53 0 0 1-1.125-.458 1.532 1.532 0 0 1-.458-1.125V5.729h1.333v10.438c0 .07.024.128.073.177a.24.24 0 0 0 .177.073h7.937v1.333H4.875ZM7.708 3.667v9.666-9.666Z" fill="#1a73e8"/></svg></div><div jscontroller="M2lJBf" jsaction="rcuQ6b:npT2md" data-enable-content-editable-input-style="false" data-enable-line-wrapping data-read-only><div class="hg3Lgc qs41qe BEXrzd" data-loadingmessage="Loading..." jscontroller="GFartf" jsaction="animationend:kWijWc;dyRcpb:dyRcpb" data-active="true" jsname="aZ2wEe"><div class="eBrXtc" aria-live="polite" jsname="vyyg5">Loading...</div><div jsname="Hxlbvc" class="JdM54e"><div class="aopPX ZqnFk co39ub"><div class="e2XBBf uEtL3"><div class="kPEoYc GOJTSe"></div></div><div class="LqC3Y"><div class="kPEoYc GOJTSe"></div></div><div class="e2XBBf QR7YS"><div class="kPEoYc GOJTSe"></div></div></div><div class="aopPX fxjES Cn087"><div class="e2XBBf uEtL3"><div class="kPEoYc GOJTSe"></div></div><div class="LqC3Y"><div class="kPEoYc GOJTSe"></div></div><div class="e2XBBf QR7YS"><div class="kPEoYc GOJTSe"></div></div></div><div class="aopPX ZHXbZe hfsr6b"><div class="e2XBBf uEtL3"><div class="kPEoYc GOJTSe"></div></div><div class="LqC3Y"><div class="kPEoYc GOJTSe"></div></div><div class="e2XBBf QR7YS"><div class="kPEoYc GOJTSe"></div></div></div><div class="aopPX fDBOYb EjXFBf"><div class="e2XBBf uEtL3"><div class="kPEoYc GOJTSe"></div></div><div class="LqC3Y"><div class="kPEoYc GOJTSe"></div></div><div class="e2XBBf QR7YS"><div class="kPEoYc GOJTSe"></div></div></div></div></div><div dir="ltr"><textarea jsname="bqeLof" class="Fdco1c">-- Count the input text tokens for each product review
SELECT
  SUM(
    AI.COUNT_TOKENS(
      CONCAT(&#39;Classify the sentiment of this review as positive, negative, or neutral: &#39;, review_text),

      endpoint =&gt; &#39;gemini-3.1-flash-lite&#39;).result) AS total_input_tokens
FROM
  `my_project.my_dataset.product_reviews`;</textarea></div></div></div></section></section><section class="Wy08Ac nRhiJb-qJTHM-OWXEXe-hJDwNd nRhiJb-DbgRPb-II5mzb-cGMI2b"><div jsaction="rcuQ6b:npT2md" jscontroller="M0Q3Qb" data-is-cws-richtext="true" class=" "><p><span style="vertical-align:baseline">The count is a lower bound on input tokens. It doesn't include output or thinking tokens, the instructions each AI function adds around your input, or non-text inputs such as images. Use it to:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="list-style-type:disc;vertical-align:baseline">
<p><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">Gauge the input side of a workload</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> before you launch it.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="list-style-type:disc;vertical-align:baseline">
<p><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">Right-size your quotas</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> together with a small sample run that measures actual input and output usage.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="list-style-type:disc;vertical-align:baseline">
<p><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">Translate tokens into dollars</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> using the published </span><a href="https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-ai/pricing"><span style="text-decoration:underline;vertical-align:baseline">Gemini platform pricing</span></a><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> for your model.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3><span style="vertical-align:baseline">From tokens to budget: a worked example</span></h3>
<p><span style="vertical-align:baseline">Suppose you want to keep a project's daily AI spend around </span><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">$100</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> with the </span><a href="https://docs.cloud.google.com/gemini-enterprise-agent-platform/models/gemini/3-1-flash-lite"><span style="text-decoration:underline;vertical-align:baseline">Gemini 3.1 Flash-Lite</span></a><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> model. As of today's published pricing (BigQuery processes in batch which provides a 50% discount):</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="list-style-type:disc;vertical-align:baseline">
<p><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">Input tokens:</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> $0.125 per 1 million tokens</span></p>
</li>
<li style="list-style-type:disc;vertical-align:baseline">
<p><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">Output tokens (response + reasoning):</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> $0.75 per 1 million tokens</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><span style="vertical-align:baseline">If a small sample run shows an average </span><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">100:1 input-to-output token ratio</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline">, you can solve for a daily budget:</span></p></div></section><section class="nRhiJb-DbgRPb-II5mzb-cGMI2b"><section><div class="kg99be" jscontroller="vkZm2d" jsaction="rcuQ6b:npT2md" data-text-to-copy="Cost:   0.125 × I + 0.75 × O = 100     (I, O in millions of tokens)
Ratio:  I = 100 × O" soy-skip ssk='4:dXrt'><div jsaction="click:VTVhdd" class="GaRnv"><svg class="" viewBox="0 0 20 20" role="presentation" aria-hidden="true" height=20 widdht=20><path d="M7.979 14.667c-.458 0-.84-.153-1.146-.459a1.53 1.53 0 0 1-.458-1.125V3.938c0-.459.153-.84.458-1.146.306-.306.688-.459 1.146-.459h6.625c.445 0 .823.156 1.136.469.312.313.468.691.468 1.136v9.145c0 .445-.156.82-.468 1.125a1.564 1.564 0 0 1-1.136.459H7.979Zm0-1.334h6.625c.083 0 .15-.024.198-.073a.239.239 0 0 0 .073-.177V3.938a.265.265 0 0 0-.073-.198.268.268 0 0 0-.198-.073H7.979a.268.268 0 0 0-.198.073.266.266 0 0 0-.073.198v9.145c0 .07.024.129.073.177a.267.267 0 0 0 .198.073ZM4.875 17.75a1.53 1.53 0 0 1-1.125-.458 1.532 1.532 0 0 1-.458-1.125V5.729h1.333v10.438c0 .07.024.128.073.177a.24.24 0 0 0 .177.073h7.937v1.333H4.875ZM7.708 3.667v9.666-9.666Z" fill="#1a73e8"/></svg></div><div jscontroller="M2lJBf" jsaction="rcuQ6b:npT2md" data-enable-content-editable-input-style="false" data-enable-line-wrapping data-read-only><div class="hg3Lgc qs41qe BEXrzd" data-loadingmessage="Loading..." jscontroller="GFartf" jsaction="animationend:kWijWc;dyRcpb:dyRcpb" data-active="true" jsname="aZ2wEe"><div class="eBrXtc" aria-live="polite" jsname="vyyg5">Loading...</div><div jsname="Hxlbvc" class="JdM54e"><div class="aopPX ZqnFk co39ub"><div class="e2XBBf uEtL3"><div class="kPEoYc GOJTSe"></div></div><div class="LqC3Y"><div class="kPEoYc GOJTSe"></div></div><div class="e2XBBf QR7YS"><div class="kPEoYc GOJTSe"></div></div></div><div class="aopPX fxjES Cn087"><div class="e2XBBf uEtL3"><div class="kPEoYc GOJTSe"></div></div><div class="LqC3Y"><div class="kPEoYc GOJTSe"></div></div><div class="e2XBBf QR7YS"><div class="kPEoYc GOJTSe"></div></div></div><div class="aopPX ZHXbZe hfsr6b"><div class="e2XBBf uEtL3"><div class="kPEoYc GOJTSe"></div></div><div class="LqC3Y"><div class="kPEoYc GOJTSe"></div></div><div class="e2XBBf QR7YS"><div class="kPEoYc GOJTSe"></div></div></div><div class="aopPX fDBOYb EjXFBf"><div class="e2XBBf uEtL3"><div class="kPEoYc GOJTSe"></div></div><div class="LqC3Y"><div class="kPEoYc GOJTSe"></div></div><div class="e2XBBf QR7YS"><div class="kPEoYc GOJTSe"></div></div></div></div></div><div dir="ltr"><textarea jsname="bqeLof" class="Fdco1c">Cost:   0.125 × I + 0.75 × O = 100     (I, O in millions of tokens)
Ratio:  I = 100 × O</textarea></div></div></div></section></section><section class="Wy08Ac nRhiJb-qJTHM-OWXEXe-hJDwNd nRhiJb-DbgRPb-II5mzb-cGMI2b"><div jsaction="rcuQ6b:npT2md" jscontroller="M0Q3Qb" data-is-cws-richtext="true" class=" "><p><span style="vertical-align:baseline">Solving gives about </span><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">754 million input tokens</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> and </span><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">7.54 million output tokens</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> per day. Set </span><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">AI input tokens per day</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> and </span><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">AI output tokens per day</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> to these values to hold the project near $100/day. If a project uses models with different prices, budget per model or blend the rates.</span></p>
<h3><span style="vertical-align:baseline">Best practices for managing AI cost</span></h3>
<ul>
<li style="list-style-type:disc;vertical-align:baseline">
<p><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">Start with per-user quotas.</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> They stop one user or runaway experiment from draining the project's budget.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="list-style-type:disc;vertical-align:baseline">
<p><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">Measure before you scale.</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> Use </span><code style="vertical-align:baseline">AI.COUNT_TOKENS</code><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> to size your input, then check a small sample run in the usage chart before setting limits.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="list-style-type:disc;vertical-align:baseline">
<p><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">Mind the output side.</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> Output tokens cost more. Where a function accepts </span><code style="vertical-align:baseline">max_output_tokens</code><span style="vertical-align:baseline">, set it to bound generation length.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="list-style-type:disc;vertical-align:baseline">
<p><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">Monitor and iterate.</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> Adjust limits as real usage and budgets change.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3><span style="vertical-align:baseline">Get started</span></h3>
<p><span style="vertical-align:baseline">Token-based cost management is available now. To begin:</span></p>
<ol>
<li style="list-style-type:decimal;vertical-align:baseline">
<p><span style="vertical-align:baseline">Open </span><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">IAM &amp; Admin → </strong><a href="https://console.cloud.google.com/iam-admin/quotas/list"><strong style="text-decoration:underline;vertical-align:baseline">Quotas &amp; System Limits</strong></a><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> in the Google Cloud Console and filter by </span><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">BigQuery API</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline">.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="list-style-type:decimal;vertical-align:baseline">
<p><span style="vertical-align:baseline">Review the four </span><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">AI-related</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> </span><strong style="vertical-align:baseline">token quotas</strong><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> and set limits that match your budget.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="list-style-type:decimal;vertical-align:baseline">
<p><span style="vertical-align:baseline">Use </span><a href="https://docs.cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/standard-sql/bigqueryml-syntax-ai-count-tokens"><code style="text-decoration:underline;vertical-align:baseline">AI.COUNT_TOKENS</code></a><span style="vertical-align:baseline"> to size your input data.</span></p>
</li>
</ol>
<p><span style="vertical-align:baseline">For the full details, see the documentation on </span><a href="https://docs.cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/control-genai-costs"><span style="text-decoration:underline;vertical-align:baseline">controlling generative AI costs</span></a><span style="vertical-align:baseline">.</span></p>
<p><span style="vertical-align:baseline">With token-based guardrails in place, your teams can use generative AI in BigQuery with the cost predictability your organization needs.</span></p></div></section><section class="kcBhad"><section class="Fabbec"><span class="WrMNjb">Posted in</span><ul class="FzXI4e"><li class="I4B51b"><a href="https://cloud.google.com/blog/products/data-analytics" track-metadata-position="body"track-metadata-eventdetail="cloud.google.com/blog/products/data-analytics"track-metadata-module="tag list"track-metadata-module_headline="posted in">Data Analytics</a></li><li class="I4B51b"><a href="https://cloud.google.com/blog/products/ai-machine-learning" track-metadata-position="body"track-metadata-eventdetail="cloud.google.com/blog/products/ai-machine-learning"track-metadata-module="tag list"track-metadata-module_headline="posted in">AI &amp; Machine Learning</a></li><li class="I4B51b"><a href="https://cloud.google.com/blog/products/bigquery" track-metadata-position="body"track-metadata-eventdetail="cloud.google.com/blog/products/bigquery"track-metadata-module="tag list"track-metadata-module_headline="posted in">BigQuery</a></li></ul></section></section></div></div></div></div></div><section class="nRhiJb-DARUcf " track-metadata-module="related articles" track-metadata-module_headline="related articles"><div class="nRhiJb-DbgRPb-c5RTEf-ma6Yeb nRhiJb-DbgRPb-wNfPc-cGMI2b"><h5 class="Qwf2Db-MnozTc Qwf2Db-MnozTc-OWXEXe-MnozTc-wNfPc nRhiJb-DbgRPb-II5mzb-cGMI2b">Related articles</h5><section class="m9cUGf  HGev3   nJD2Qe  nRhiJb-ObfsIf"><div class="  QaGyvd  nRhiJb-kR0ZEf-OWXEXe-GV1x9e-c5RTEf nRhiJb-kR0ZEf-OWXEXe-GV1x9e-qWD73c-V2iZpe"><div class="mA0uBe"><a href="https://cloud.google.com/blog/products/data-analytics/cross-cloud-conversational-analytics-with-borderless-lakehouse" class="lD2oe" track-name="cross-cloud conversational analytics made simple with open standards"track-type="card"track-metadata-eventdetail="cloud.google.com/blog/products/data-a